Error [jet.CollectionChangedWhileRead]: While the loop is reading `names`, nothing may change it
  --> tests/ui/list_loop_lend_for_write.jet:10:19
    |
 10 |         clear_all(names)
    |                   ^^^^^
 Why: The loop reads `names` across its body, so lending `names` for writing to `clear_all` can change the visited domain, element order, or termination.
 Fix: Choose the collection intent explicitly: use a separate result when the original traversal should stay unchanged; snapshot `names` and iterate the fixed original set when only the original values belong in the traversal; or use an explicit work queue when newly added values should be visited. Do not use index traversal unless its fixed domain and result meaning are intended.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0507
